# Ecosystem architecture (MatchPoint SBOM stack)

Read **AGENTS.md** in this repo before changing EDK2 or assembly behavior.

## Ownership

| Layer | Repo | Owns |
|-------|------|------|
| SBOM creation | **python-uswid-sbom** (`uswid`) | `--primary-dir`, `uswid/submodule.py`, `uswid/edk2.py`, format writers, UEFI compliance |
| CVE analysis | **SBOM4EDK2** | NVD, Grype, GHSA, `generate_sbom_from_checkout` (thin `uswid` subprocess only) |
| Quarterly VEX | **VEX4EDK2** | `vex4edk2.batch`, CSAF writer, `releases/` artifacts |

## Forbidden in downstream repos (SBOM4EDK2, VEX4EDK2)

- Per-`.inf` thread pools, manual CycloneDX merge, `_merge_inf_cdx_direct`-style helpers
- Duplicating `walk_gitmodules`, `normalize_submodule_version`, or `@VCS_*@` substitution
- Importing `uswid.edk2` from production orchestration code in those repos

## Forbidden in this repo (python-uswid-sbom)

- CVE/NVD/GHSA scanning or CSAF VEX batch logic
- Git clone orchestration for quarterly releases (belongs in VEX4EDK2)

## Module seam in this repo

- **Generic:** `uswid/submodule.py` — no EDK2 references
- **EDK2-only:** `uswid/edk2.py` — not imported by `uswid/cli.py`
- New EDK2 assembly behavior → extend `--primary-dir` / `submodule.py`, not SBOM4EDK2

## Fork edits

Append-only on `cli.py`, `component.py`, `entity.py`, `format_cyclonedx.py`, `format_spdx.py` when possible. Do not edit upstream-identical files without explicit direction.
